The array is `n + 1` slots. The maximum index written is `n` (when `i` was `n-1` and gets incremented to `n` in the outer loop's `points[i++] = first;`). Wait, in the outer loop, `i < n` is the condition. So when entering the loop, `i <= n-1`. Then `points[i++] = first;` writes to index `i` (which is `<= n-1`) and increments `i`. So max index written in the outer loop is `n-1`.

In the inner loop, `points[i++] = first;` is executed before the `if ( i >= n ) break;`. So if `i` was `n-1`, then `points[n-1] = first; i = n;` then break. So max index is `n-1`.

So the max index written is `n-1`, within the `n+1` allocation. Safe.

